  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multi-profile with PCA n2000 and avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the strongest result so far, showing a ~10.6% gain over single-profile (config_001, acc=0.485). Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the RNA pathway is the clear direction to exploit. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether a transformer aggregation can capture inter-profile interactions beyond simple averaging, which could push accuracy further. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding RNA encoder (PCA n2000), profile setting (multiprofile), and modality (RNA-only) constant, giving a clean isolation of the aggregation effect. It is the best next step because it directly exploits the strongest signal found so far, answers a high-value design question with minimal confounding, and will inform whether to invest remaining budget in transformer-based aggregation across other encoders and multimodal settings."
}

